{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970743-fate-sight-ideas","id":970743,"title":"Fate Sight Ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-16T09:26:15-07:00","id":970743,"title":"Fate Sight Ideas","content":"Hi folks. Been having trouble coming up with Fate Sight descriptions for my Acanthus player. Core book talks about threads and such, but I'm not quite sold on that. How would you describe the promising (or terrible) destiny of someone through the lens of Fate? How about when viewing objects or places? Hope to hear your examples!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T12:49:34-07:00","id":970850,"title":"","content":"I have two players with Fate Sight, an Acanthus and an Obrimos. I've found that my players really aren't interested in hearing or offering flowery, poetic description of what Mage Sight looks like, which is fine, so I keep it brief and practical. One thing I enjoy doing is that when I know something story-important is about to happen and they have Fate Sight up, I'll say something like &quot;You feel a sense of anticipation. A hush falls over the crowd of watching Fae, there's a quiet drumroll. Something big is about to go down.&quot;<br /> <br /> If they saw a character with a Destiny, I would probably say something like this.<br /> Obrimos: &quot;The woman in front of the crowd is incandescent with potential energy. Like entropy, there is an end state she cannot avoid. She has a Destiny.&quot;<br /> Acanthus: &quot;The woman in front of the crowd stands out as if the camera was focused on her. She's a lead singer, and the people around her are backup dancers. She has a Destiny.&quot;<br /> <br /> If they wanted more details about what the Destiny actually was, they'd want to use Scrutiny/Revelation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T18:08:25-07:00","id":971036,"title":"","content":"Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> that's some pretty evocative narration. I'll try it out next session, just to give variety to the Acanthus experience. Regarding the Fae, how do you describe them? Are they just standing around, mouth agape, watching the person with Destiny?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T18:51:45-07:00","id":971069,"title":"","content":"I'd describe them similarly to the way they are in stories. Usually doing something. If there are Fae hanging around a person with Destiny though, Supernal beings ahoy!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T16:59:09-07:00","id":971583,"title":"","content":"Maybe, something like seeing people and things for the &quot;roles&quot; they play according to Fate/the Wyrd? So, more important objects or people look more distinctive/dramatic. A teacher who lords over his class like a tyrant sports a top hat and long thin mustache. The football star in his class appears as a knight in shining armor, and when they argue the Mage sees flashes of them with swords drawn and lightning sparking around them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T19:13:05-07:00","id":971668,"title":"","content":"Besides the path, Mage Sight is a personal experience. Even if you have not discussed with your players exaustivelly, their Shadow Name, Nimbus and Awakening might be the lenses through which can See The Truth.<br /> <br /> Continuing Caladriu's woman example:<br /> <br /> Imagine Thor, the Obrimos. Nimbus of Thundering Sounds of Umquestionable Truth. Awakened through mystery play while watching the Avengers<br /> &quot;You can feel a sudden surge, as Bifrost opens your divine senses. The woman infront of you carries the Mark of Asguard; a thunderstorm raging above and around her. The gods have empowered her with destiny&quot; (Thunders of Asguard = power to shape Truths)<br /> <br /> Imagine Hecate, the Acanthus. Nimbus of Phrophetic Omens of Sealed Destiny. Awakened engulfed by the mists of Acadia<br /> &quot;Thick mist beginns to form, while a crow cocks suddenly once. Everyone seems to be lost in the fog. Everyone exept this woman. The mist clears around her as she walks, guiding her into her predesposed destiny&quot; (lost in fog = insignificance, clearing of mist = cosmic importance)<br /> <br /> Imagine Cumberbatch, the Mastigos. Nimbus of Satisfaction from Revealed Secrets. Awakened by investigating his projected Oneiros, filtered by Pandemonium<br /> &quot;You can now See through anyone as you did once with yourself. Everyone is guided by somone's urges, if not his/her own. Anyone but she. With an investigative glimpse you realise from her pattern that she can shape the urges of anyone she comes in contact with, immune even by her own. That does't mean she knows it though&quot; (urges = distraction, immunity = focused astral destination = Her astral path starts to converge)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","name":"Shadowjim12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T02:14:41-07:00","id":971843,"title":"","content":"Cool descrpitions Caladriu and Shadowjim12 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T02:21:41-07:00","id":971845,"title":"","content":"Excellent job you nailed the Obrimos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T10:55:18-07:00","id":972014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>terpsichordean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970743-fate-sight-ideas?p=971036#post971036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> that's some pretty evocative narration. I'll try it out next session, just to give variety to the Acanthus experience. Regarding the Fae, how do you describe them? Are they just standing around, mouth agape, watching the person with Destiny?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more of a descriptive aspect of the scenery than a literal group of characters that are present. Mage Sight involves looking into the Supernal World, so it's understood that there are Supernal beings present along with the symbols that pass information to the mage. You don't need to be like &quot;this is what the Greek chorus is doing right now&quot; every time they turn on Mage Sight, just bring it up as description when relevant.<br /> <br /> Different example. I once had a Moros with Matter Sight active while he cast some Matter 1 spell to determine the purity of a sample of coke, and I described him seeing Anubis weighing the coke against a feather on a set of scales. You can use Supernal beings to make the sight more dynamic, but they don't need to be active participants in the scene. (Unless you dramatic fail a Scrutiny roll, or do some other interesting emergent magical thing to make them screw with you using their powers)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}